WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:03.990
I open a finding from the Deslop

00:03.990 --> 00:07.681
sidebar. Its details show the files containing

00:07.681 --> 00:11.371
the repeated code. I can follow either

00:11.371 --> 00:15.061
file link to see the original source,

00:15.061 --> 00:18.751
without leaving the editor or copying line

00:18.751 --> 00:20.860
numbers into a search.

00:21.660 --> 00:24.268
I click the comparison button beside the

00:24.268 --> 00:26.877
second copy. Deslop opens both files together,

00:26.877 --> 00:29.485
with their differences highlighted. I can read

00:29.485 --> 00:32.094
the same section on each side and

00:32.094 --> 00:34.702
check whether the differences matter before I

00:34.702 --> 00:35.820
change either file.

00:36.620 --> 00:39.592
When I want a different pair, I

00:39.592 --> 00:42.565
select one copy first, then choose Compare

00:42.565 --> 00:45.537
with Selected on the other. The editor

00:45.537 --> 00:48.509
opens those two files together. I can

00:48.509 --> 00:51.482
repeat this for another pair when a

00:51.482 --> 00:53.180
finding contains several copies.

00:53.980 --> 00:56.087
Back in the sidebar, I expand Duplication

00:56.087 --> 00:58.193
to see the project and file totals.

00:58.193 --> 01:00.300
The file rows help me choose where

01:00.300 --> 01:02.407
to investigate next. I open a file

01:02.407 --> 01:04.513
from that list, then return to its

01:04.513 --> 01:06.620
finding to review the actual repeated code.
